  "claude": {
    "enabled": true,
    "research": {
      "notes": "**Palantir (PLTR): news for 2026-09-15 to 2026-10-15**\n\n**1. Guidance and results**\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal turned up in the window. The latest guidance is from the Q2 report. Next earnings date is unconfirmed (MarketBeat estimates 2026-11-02). Dates are given as the source states them.\n- FY26 revenue guidance was raised to $8.150–8.158B, with Q3 revenue guided to $2.160–2.164B. Also raised: U.S. commercial revenue to above $3.424B, adjusted operating income to $4.889–4.897B, and adjusted free cash flow to $4.5–4.7B. — 2026-08-03 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001321655/000132165526000039/a2026q2ex991pressrelease.htm\n- Q2 revenue was $1.94B against about $1.80B expected, and adjusted EPS was $0.41 against $0.35 expected. — 2026-08-03 — https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/03/palantir-pltr-earnings-q2-2026.html\n- Q2 EPS consensus was $0.34 per MarketBeat and $1.81B for revenue, slightly different from CNBC's figures. — 2026-08-03 — https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/PLTR/earnings/\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- Goldman Sachs (Gabriela Borges) upgraded to Buy from Neutral with a $230 target. — 2026-10-08 — https://www.thestreet.com/investing/stocks/pltr-palantir-technologies-stock-12-month-price-target-raised-by-18-percent-goldman-sachs-october-2026\n- Goldman's estimates are $8.37B revenue for 2026 and $13.2B for 2027. — 2026-10-08 — same TheStreet URL.\n- Barclays (Anthony Valentini) initiated at Buy with a $265 target. — 2026-10-08 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/pltr/forecast/\n- Robert W. Baird (William Power) kept Buy and raised its target to $250 from $200. — 2026-10-12 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/pltr/forecast/\n- Phillip Securities (Paul Chew) downgraded to Hold with a $215 target. — 2026-10-12 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/pltr/forecast/\n- I could not find a primary source for these four actions beyond the Goldman coverage and the aggregator table. The Barclays, Baird and Phillip entries rest on a single aggregator.\n\n**3. Litigation and regulation**\n- Palantir settled its lawsuit against the London mayor's policing office (MOPAC) over a blocked £50M (about $66M) Metropolitan Police contract. Both sides withdrew their allegations. — 2026-10-14 — https://1027wbow.com/2026/10/14/palantir-and-london-mayors-office-settle-lawsuit-over-uk-police-contract/ (Reuters syndication)\n- The UK is reviewing Palantir's £330M NHS contract. A parliamentary committee cited a \"clear mismatch with UK values\" and recommended using a break clause. Palantir's UK CEO called that \"irresponsible\". — 2026-10-14 (date of the report; the committee's date is unknown) — https://www.newarab.com/news/palantir-and-london-mayor-settle-lawsuit-over-uk-police-contract\n- No new fines, antitrust actions or export-control actions were found in the window.\n\n**4. Customers and contracts**\n- The U.S. Army awarded TITAN production delivery orders worth $192M to Palantir and Anduril. Palantir leads, and Anduril handles hardware and shelter integration. — 2026-09-02 (article date; award date unknown) — https://www.govconwire.com/articles/palantir-anduril-army-titan-192m-production-orders\n- This item is outside the window. The Army expanded its Maven Smart System contract by $618M, and the Maven ceiling rose to about $1.3B. — 2026-08-25 — https://app.govly.com/public/signals/177815\n- Concentration: government was $990M of $1,935M Q2 revenue (about 51%). U.S. government revenue was $809M. — Q2 2026 (quarter ended 2026-06-30) — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001321655/000132165526000041/pltr-20260630.htm\n- I found no customer losses in the window apart from the blocked London contract above.\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- Director Alexander Moore sold 16,000 shares at about $170–176 under a 10b5-1 plan adopted 2025-12-11. — 2026-09-15 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/PLTR/form-4-palantir-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-4df8b55709ce.html\n- Chief Revenue Officer and Chief Legal Officer Ryan Taylor sold 18,000 shares at $201.15 (about $3.62M). The Form 4 summary lists it as a 10b5-1 sale. — 2026-10-08 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/PLTR/form-4-palantir-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-0a6ea37c1408.html\n- Director Lauren Friedman Stat sold 5,026 shares at $199 (about $1.0M) under a plan adopted 2026-02-11. — 2026-10-08 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/PLTR/form-4-palantir-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-ccc1e1cede6b.html\n- The two 2026-10-08 sales are a small cluster. No insider purchases were found.\n- The CEO's tax-cover sales of 492,348 shares, about $86M, fall outside the window. — 2026-08-20 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/PLTR/form-4-palantir-technologies-inc-insider-trading-activity-c654c12a92fa.html\n\n**6. Product and competition**\n- Palantir made xAI's Grok 4.7 available to eligible AIP commercial customers. This fits its approach of supporting several AI model providers. — 2026-09-24 — https://www.thestreet.com/investing/palantirs-latest-ai-move-reveals-a-much-bigger-ambition\n- Goldman lists three risks: competitors replicating Palantir's forward-deployed-engineer model, slower enterprise AI adoption, and (a third risk the article cuts off). — 2026-10-08 — https://www.thestreet.com/investing/stocks/pltr-palantir-technologies-stock-12-month-price-target-raised-by-18-percent-goldman-sachs-october-2026\n- No pricing changes, delays or new-competitor announcements were found.\n\n**Stock context**\n- Shares closed at $194.12 on 2026-10-07, hit a 52-week high of about $209, and were around $200 on 2026-10-14 to 2026-10-15. — https://www.fxleaders.com/news/2026/10/14/pltr-stock-falls-to-100-as-ai-financing-risks-spread-across-tech-and-analysts-review-palantir-technologies-valuation-and-target-prices/",
